		{
			dependencies: [
				"72D090FF4C44DAAD"
				"3FED9C9227FC9CD5"
			]
			description: [
				"1.In the position indicated by the &cred box&r in the image below, we can see which mod an item  belongs to."
				"&7— As shown, the item in the image comes from the mod “Nameless Trinkets”&r"
				"{image:kubejs:textures/task/jei_1.png width:124 height:47 align:1}"
				""
				""
				"2.If you want to see what items a mod contains, press &eE&r to open your inventory, then type &e“@+mod name”&r in the &eJEI search box in the bottom-right corner&r. For example, you can type &e“@Nameless”&r to search for the mod shown in the previous image."
				"{image:kubejs:textures/task/jei_2.png width:160 height:15 align:1}"
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"3.Normally, you can directly search for an item’s name in the JEI search bar, then &eleft-click&r it to view how to craft it (or hover over the item and press &eR – Show Recipe&r)."
				"Hovering over an item and pressing &eU (Show Uses)&r allows you to see what it can be used for. If the item has crafting functions, all supported recipes will be displayed."
				"&7(As shown below: when hovering over the red-marked area in Image 1 and pressing U, the summoning altar provides crafting methods for other items, so its recipes are shown.)&r"
				"{image:kubejs:textures/task/jei_3.png width:130 height:68 align:1}"
				"{image:kubejs:textures/task/jei_4.png width:105 height:99 align:1}"
			]
			icon: "minecraft:writable_book"
			id: "55A4D2A38D0297E8"
			rewards: [{
				id: "2F0F6E4BA49B55C1"
				item: "lightmanscurrency:coin_iron"
				type: "item"
			}]
